[Distributed correctness findings]
- Atomicity is per partition/Raft log/RocksDB WriteBatch, not per nGQL statement.
- Cross-partition or cross-host partial commits are possible; mutation execution
  rejects partial success but does not roll back successful partitions.
- E_LEADER_CHANGED updates graphd's local leader cache for a later request; the
  addVertices call itself is not resubmitted by StorageClient.
- E_RAFT_UNKNOWN_APPEND_LOG is an indeterminate result: a replicated log may
  later be committed by a new leader.
- Native tag-index rows and primary tag rows share the same partition batch.
- Elasticsearch listeners are learners and do not participate in write quorum;
  full-text visibility can lag nGQL success.
- IF NOT EXISTS is not a strict compare-and-set in either write path. The indexed
  path does not represent an absent old row in its read set, and concurrent
  write/write operations retain last-write-wins behavior.

